A", "B"], "count": 2}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "enqueue", "label": "B", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "C cannot be accepted yet. Its producer suspends and holds C; no item travels into the full queue.", "set": {"nodes": {"producer": ["is-warn", "C pending; suspended"]}}}, {"caption": "The consumer takes A. B remains pending; A is now processing outside the queue.", "set": {"nodes": {"queue": ["", "1 / 2: B"], "consumer": ["is-active", "processing A"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": ["B"], "count": 1}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "dequeue", "label": "A", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "The waiting send resumes and C is accepted. Pending items are B, C; A is still the consumer’s current item.", "set": {"nodes": {"producer": ["is-done", "C accepted"], "queue": ["is-active", "2 / 2: B, C"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": ["B", "C"], "count": 2}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "enqueue", "label": "C", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}]}, "drop": {"initial": {"nodes": {"producer": ["", "A, then B, then C"], "queue": ["", "0 / 2 pending"], "consumer": ["", "not taking yet"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": [], "count": 0}}}, "steps": [{"caption": "Start with an empty two-slot queue and a consumer that has not taken an item.", "set": {"nodes": {"producer": ["is-active", "A, then B, then C"]}}}, {"caption": "A is accepted. One of two pending slots is occupied.", "set": {"nodes": {"queue": ["is-active", "1 / 2: A"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": ["A"], "count": 1}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "enqueue", "label": "A", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "B is accepted. The queue is now full: A, B.", "set": {"nodes": {"queue": ["is-warn", "2 / 2: A, B"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": ["A", "B"], "count": 2}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "enqueue", "label": "B", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "C arrives under DROP_OLDEST. A is discarded before processing; C is accepted. The producer does not wait.", "set": {"nodes": {"producer": ["is-done", "C accepted"], "queue": ["is-warn", "2 / 2: B, C; A dropped"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": ["B", "C"], "count": 2}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "enqueue", "label": "C", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "The consumer takes B. C remains pending. The dropped A cannot be reconstructed from this queue.", "set": {"nodes": {"queue": ["", "1 / 2: C"], "consumer": ["is-active", "processing B"]}, "visuals": {"queue": {"items": ["C"], "count": 1}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "dequeue", "label": "B", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}]}}}</script>
</section>

The queue's capacity counts pending items, not the item already being processed or held by a suspended producer. This example preserves order among accepted items. Drop-oldest removes an unprocessed item; it does not cancel the consumer's current work.

[Sources: buffer's suspension and overflow rules](https://kotlinlang.org/api/kotlinx.coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-core/kotlinx.coroutines.flow/buffer.html), [conflate's pending-value behavior](https://kotlinlang.org/api/kotlinx.coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-core/kotlinx.coroutines.flow/conflate.html).

<!-- @after Failure Modes :: staff -->
### Find the boundary that stopped cooperating

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Callback["Non-suspending source"]
      Sensor["Sensor callback"]
    end
    subgraph Bridge["Explicit admission boundary"]
      Offer["Try bounded admission"]
      Decide["Reject, replace or persist according to contract"]
    end
    Queue["Bounded pending work"]
    Consumer["Processing owner"]
    Sensor -->|"new sample"| Offer
    Offer -->|"accepted"| Queue
    Offer -->|"full or unavailable"| Decide
    Queue -->|"dequeue"| Consumer
    Consumer -.->|"available capacity controls next admission"| Offer
```

A dispatcher change is not the boundary that breaks backpressure: a coroutine on another dispatcher can still suspend. An unbounded series of `launch` calls around `send` is different; it relocates the backlog into waiting coroutines. Measure queue age, in-flight work and dropped values, not queue length alone.
